From ca7775d58c0900e1fad5f7d75d2c869438f4abea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: <worker git identity, redacted>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:45:46 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Never clean up a worktree recreated at the same path

Worktree identity compared the admin directory path and the inode numbers
of that directory and the `.git` file. ext4 hands freed inode numbers
straight back, so a worktree that someone removed and recreated at the
same path matched the recorded identity and cleanup offered
`git worktree remove` for it.

Recording a run-owned worktree now writes a random owner token into its
admin directory (.git/worktrees/<name>/t3-owner). `git worktree remove`
and `prune` delete that directory, so a recreated worktree never carries
the token and is reported as replaced. Identities recorded before tokens
were kept are still compared on their recorded keys.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
